#### Run Your Code

Once you've prepared everything, you can now build and run your code.

First, follow the [Build and Run iOS Lynx Explorer](https://github.com/lynx-family/lynx/tree/develop/explorer/darwin/ios#build-ios-app) guide to build Lynx Explorer and install it on your phone.

Next, refer to the [Install Dependencies & Start the Development Server](/next/guide/start/quick-start.md#start-developing) guide to install dependencies and start the development server in the root directory of your Lynx project.

Install dependencies:


```sh [npm]
npm install
```

```sh [yarn]
yarn install
```

```sh [pnpm]
pnpm install
```

```sh [bun]
bun install
```

```sh [deno]
deno install
```

Start the development server:


```sh [npm]
npm run dev
```

```sh [yarn]
yarn run dev
```

```sh [pnpm]
pnpm run dev
```

```sh [bun]
bun run dev
```

```sh [deno]
deno run npm:dev
```

You'll see a QR code and an artifact link in the console. Use Lynx Explorer to scan the QR code or enter the artifact link to open your Lynx page.

